Unit tests, run on the computer (no ESP needed):

    pio test -e native

- test_firmware/test_main.cpp : the tests. It includes src/main.cpp unchanged.
- mocks/ : fake Arduino core, Wi-Fi, Wi-Fi manager, LittleFS, ESP Async
  WebServer, ArduinoOTA, Updater and PubSubClient (MQTT) headers. They
  record GPIO writes and delays, and let a test call a URL or send an
  MQTT message.

More info: https://docs.platformio.org/en/latest/advanced/unit-testing/index.html
